From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:45:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: allocate the first TEB only for a thread that has none

wine-11.18 allocates the first TEB and the PEB in init_startup_info.
A pseudo-process child runs that function too, from wine_ios_child_main,
after it gave the child's thread a TEB, a stack and a PEB of its own:
the child's thread data then pointed at a fresh TEB with no stack, the
session's peb global moved to a new block, and the child's first thread
faulted in init_syscall_frame (a memmove to StackBase 0 - 0x3a0).
virtual_alloc_first_teb now returns when the calling thread already
has a TEB, which only a child's has; the session's first process
allocates them as before.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-child-process.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 8e13106..242974b 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -15361,6 +15361,15 @@ void virtual_alloc_first_teb(void)
     struct thread_data *data = get_thread_data();
     ULONG_PTR limit_low = 0, limit_high = 0;
 
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    /* Playport: the first TEB and the PEB beside it are made once, for the
+     * session's first process. A pseudo-process child runs init_startup_info
+     * too (wine_ios_child_main), on a thread that already has its TEB, stack
+     * and PEB; allocating here replaced that TEB with a stackless one and
+     * moved the peb global to a fresh block, and the child's first thread
+     * faulted in init_syscall_frame. A thread that has a TEB keeps it. */
+    if (data->teb) return;
+#endif
     set_large_address_space();
 
     teb_block_size = ROUND_SIZE( 0, sizeof(TEB), page_mask );
